00:38:40.250 --> 00:38:43.310
Like a notebook from Nellie's desk notebook.

1049
00:38:44.190 --> 00:38:46.010
But did it have your real scribbles in it?

1050
00:38:46.130 --> 00:38:46.430
Yes.

1051
00:38:46.650 --> 00:38:48.130
It had my real scribbles in it.

1052
00:38:50.330 --> 00:38:51.850
And it had on it.

1053
00:38:52.250 --> 00:38:55.210
And because we went online and looked, because I was like, oh, my God, you better.

1054
00:38:55.330 --> 00:38:56.770
I said to my husband, you better buy that.

1055
00:38:57.150 --> 00:39:01.130
Because can you imagine if I'm going, I'm so bored.

1056
00:39:01.950 --> 00:39:05.800
I didn't know what I was going to say.

1057
00:39:06.560 --> 00:39:07.980
And we looked online.

1058
00:39:08.680 --> 00:39:09.800
And do you know what?

1059
00:39:09.920 --> 00:39:13.400
One of the things we could zoom in and see was an address.

1060
00:39:13.940 --> 00:39:14.560
Oh, no.

1061
00:39:14.800 --> 00:39:15.860
It was an address.

1062
00:39:16.380 --> 00:39:17.340
And do you know what it was?

1063
00:39:17.680 --> 00:39:20.840
It was the place of our first date.

1064
00:39:21.520 --> 00:39:21.880
What?

1065
00:39:22.120 --> 00:39:22.880
Isn't that crazy?

1066
00:39:23.660 --> 00:39:25.340
Like you had written it.

1067
00:39:25.460 --> 00:39:26.220
I'd written down.

1068
00:39:26.360 --> 00:39:27.660
And this is when we were friends.

1069
00:39:27.920 --> 00:39:28.940
We were just friends.

1070
00:39:29.100 --> 00:39:30.000
I shouldn't say date.

1071
00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:33.640
But I remember the time and him going, oh, do you want to?

1072
00:39:33.760 --> 00:39:34.400
Because he's a writer.

1073
00:39:34.540 --> 00:39:36.000
And I was like, oh, I'm writing this show.

1074
00:39:36.120 --> 00:39:36.680
Do you want to do it?

1075
00:39:36.700 --> 00:39:39.820
Because he was a dad from the school and blah, blah, blah.

1076
00:39:40.980 --> 00:39:43.900
And I remember we met at this Tex-Mex place.

1077
00:39:44.600 --> 00:39:45.820
And I still didn't eat a taco.

1078
00:39:47.980 --> 00:39:49.140
I was like, I'll have a salad.

1079
00:39:49.380 --> 00:39:50.980
But that is so amazing.

1080
00:39:51.180 --> 00:39:52.520
That's that moment in time.

1081
00:39:52.520 --> 00:39:56.720
It had the Tex-Mex address at like 8 p.m.

1082
00:39:57.380 --> 00:39:58.460
Isn't that funny?

1083
00:39:58.700 --> 00:40:01.260
That is so crazy.

1084
00:40:01.760 --> 00:40:02.700
Did you get the book?

1085
00:40:02.700 --> 00:40:03.120
Your first meeting.

1086
00:40:03.560 --> 00:40:03.960
No.

1087
00:40:04.560 --> 00:40:06.240
He wouldn't bid enough for it.

1088
00:40:08.520 --> 00:40:13.100
Were you surprised when you came on the show how much background work we had to do?

1089
00:40:13.220 --> 00:40:15.900
How much you had to sit in the background of other people's stuff?

1090
00:40:15.940 --> 00:40:16.160
Oh, my God.

1091
00:40:16.300 --> 00:40:16.420
Yes.

1092
00:40:16.420 --> 00:40:17.480
Did anyone warn you?

1093
00:40:17.700 --> 00:40:18.200
No.

1094
00:40:18.640 --> 00:40:19.960
I did not know.

1095
00:40:20.220 --> 00:40:21.760
We were there all the time.

1096
00:40:22.160 --> 00:40:22.620
All the time.

1097
00:40:22.620 --> 00:40:24.940
But of course, that's what made the show.

1098
00:40:25.180 --> 00:40:28.880
Because we felt like we lived there and we worked there and we were these people.

1099
00:40:29.340 --> 00:40:33.940
And actually, it would have been such a different experience if all you did was these isolated scenes.

1100
00:40:34.160 --> 00:40:34.480
Oh, for sure.

1101
00:40:34.740 --> 00:40:36.280
It would have just not been the same.

1102
00:40:36.400 --> 00:40:37.980
But at the time, it was literally.

1103
00:40:38.220 --> 00:40:41.100
And because a lot of the time I was with Stanley and Phyllis.

1104
00:40:41.240 --> 00:40:41.400
Yeah.

1105
00:40:41.740 --> 00:40:45.400
And I remember her saying, which is true, you know, she always used to have her signs in her desk.

1106
00:40:45.840 --> 00:40:46.600
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

1107
00:40:47.200 --> 00:40:51.160
And they would always, they would get me into these habits of going,

1108
00:40:51.160 --> 00:40:54.600
and just, you know, just put the sweets in your desk, the candy.

1109
00:40:54.720 --> 00:40:55.020
Yes.

1110
00:40:55.660 --> 00:40:56.300
In your desk.

1111
00:40:56.840 --> 00:40:58.600
And they'd fill up their thing with Coke.

1112
00:40:59.020 --> 00:40:59.200
Yeah.

1113
00:41:00.000 --> 00:41:04.980
I would go over to Phyllis's desk, open her drawer, look at her sides and grab a Tootsie Roll.

1114
00:41:05.120 --> 00:41:05.380
Right.

1115
00:41:05.540 --> 00:41:06.140
Right, right, right.

1116
00:41:07.060 --> 00:41:08.240
Oh, so good.

1117
00:41:08.460 --> 00:41:09.080
Yeah, so good.

1118
00:41:09.180 --> 00:41:14.220
And I guess, yeah, the other thing I took from the office was what I didn't expect when I left the office

1119
00:41:14.220 --> 00:41:19.820
was that I have an American life now because I met my husband, not at the office,

1120
00:41:19.940 --> 00:41:22.680
but I met my husband because I was over here living.

1121
00:41:22.840 --> 00:41:23.480
During that time.

1122
00:41:23.640 --> 00:41:24.280
During that time.

1123
00:41:24.360 --> 00:41:24.460
Yeah.

1124
00:41:24.640 --> 00:41:26.660
And it wasn't until, you know, years later we got together.

1125
00:41:26.660 --> 00:41:31.080
But had I not got that job and lived in that place and my daughter gone to that school.

1126
00:41:31.500 --> 00:41:31.760
Yeah.

1127
00:41:32.080 --> 00:41:32.500
Crazy.

1128
00:41:33.080 --> 00:41:33.480
Yeah.

1129
00:41:33.820 --> 00:41:34.440
It's meant to be.

1130
00:41:34.580 --> 00:41:35.000
I know.

1131
00:41:35.360 --> 00:41:35.920
It's meant to be.

1132
00:41:36.460 --> 00:41:38.640
Angela, do you want to ask your call sheet questions?

1133
00:41:38.840 --> 00:41:39.400
I do.

1134
00:41:39.620 --> 00:41:40.880
I love them so much.

1135
00:41:41.060 --> 00:41:42.340
So here we go.

1136
00:41:42.560 --> 00:41:42.720
Okay.

1137
00:41:43.040 --> 00:41:46.960
Number one, what was your first entertainment job?

1138
00:41:47.480 --> 00:41:49.160
Meaning the one I got paid for.

1139
00:41:50.100 --> 00:41:50.540
Sure.

1140
00:41:50.760 --> 00:41:50.860
Sure.

1141
00:41:51.020 --> 00:41:53.160
Or just the one I found most entertaining.

1142
00:41:53.640 --> 00:41:54.820
Your first one.

1143
00:41:54.820 --> 00:41:56.520
What springs to mind.

1144
00:41:56.840 --> 00:42:04.220
I think it would have been on a show before I went to college and it was a sitcom called

1145
00:42:04.960 --> 00:42:05.800
Surgical Spirit.

1146
00:42:06.460 --> 00:42:06.880
Oh.

1147
00:42:07.240 --> 00:42:08.800
And I was someone's girlfriend.

1148
00:42:09.100 --> 00:42:11.440
Like the mom in it had a son and I was his girlfriend.

1149
00:42:11.720 --> 00:42:15.000
I think that's the thing I would have got my first paycheck from.

1150
00:42:15.440 --> 00:42:16.600
And how old were you?

1151
00:42:16.760 --> 00:42:18.280
I would have been like 18.

1152
00:42:18.700 --> 00:42:19.240
Oh, wow.

1153
00:42:19.340 --> 00:42:23.000
And did you already know entertainment was what you wanted to do with your life at that point?

1154
00:42:23.000 --> 00:42:26.440
I definitely did because I deferred a year when I got into drama school.

1155
00:42:26.680 --> 00:42:30.300
So I had a whole year before I knew I was going and this was the summer before.

1156
00:42:30.560 --> 00:42:34.760
So I like walked into college with like TV credit.

1157
00:42:34.960 --> 00:42:35.280
Yeah.

1158
00:42:35.440 --> 00:42:36.420
I've been on the television.

1159
00:42:38.200 --> 00:42:39.100
Did you even?

1160
00:42:39.180 --> 00:42:40.040
You barely needed.

1161
00:42:40.160 --> 00:42:40.380
Right.

1162
00:42:40.560 --> 00:42:41.940
I mean, what can you tell me?

1163
00:42:42.180 --> 00:42:42.400
Yeah.

1164
00:42:42.680 --> 00:42:43.340
I've done it all.

1165
00:42:43.380 --> 00:42:44.260
In your three year course.

1166
00:42:45.480 --> 00:42:46.040
All right.

1167
00:42:46.200 --> 00:42:46.820
Next question.

1168
00:42:46.980 --> 00:42:48.900
Do you speak any other languages?

1169
00:43:00.680 --> 00:43:02.220
Oh, that was wonderful.

1170
00:43:02.780 --> 00:43:04.480
How did you come to speak so many languages?

1171
00:43:04.840 --> 00:43:05.840
Well, do you know what it was?

1172
00:43:05.920 --> 00:43:10.220
I think it comes back to wanting to be an actor because I realized I like to do voices.

1173
00:43:10.660 --> 00:43:17.360
And I also realized that I was able to pick up languages very quickly because I was able to imitate the accent quite quickly.

1174
00:43:17.360 --> 00:43:25.280
It boosted me because people thought I could speak better than I could and it boosted me to do better actually than I did.

1175
00:43:25.460 --> 00:43:31.220
But French I speak pretty fluently because I studied in France and lived in France.

1176
00:43:31.220 --> 00:43:35.840
I lived in Spain for a bit because I was a nanny when I was about 19.

1177
00:43:35.840 --> 00:43:40.080
I was a nanny in Madrid and I used to have an Italian boyfriend.

1178
00:43:40.080 --> 00:43:46.780
And because if you've got one of the sort of those languages, they kind of branch off pretty quick, especially Spanish and Italian.

1179
00:43:47.120 --> 00:43:50.280
If you're learning them, it's kind of easy to see the pieces.

1180
00:43:50.520 --> 00:43:57.000
But I've just got that brain for sort of languages in a way that I don't have a brain for like maths or indeed driving.

1181
00:43:59.000 --> 00:43:59.820
Oh, my gosh.

1182
00:43:59.960 --> 00:44:00.940
I'm not spatially aware.

1183
00:44:01.100 --> 00:44:02.480
But, yeah, I can pick up a language.

1184
00:44:02.980 --> 00:44:03.320
All right.

1185
00:44:03.620 --> 00:44:04.740
Question number three.

1186
00:44:05.680 --> 00:44:09.080
What's a place you've been to that you absolutely loved?

1187
00:44:09.080 --> 00:44:10.420
Oh, my goodness.

1188
00:44:10.640 --> 00:44:11.800
There's a lot.

1189
00:44:11.880 --> 00:44:12.360
There's a lot.

1190
00:44:12.440 --> 00:44:12.900
There's a lot.

1191
00:44:13.020 --> 00:44:16.680
I have to say New Zealand is pretty amazing.

1192
00:44:17.040 --> 00:44:20.160
And I also love, I love Australia.

1193
00:44:20.780 --> 00:44:21.040
Yeah.

1194
00:44:21.240 --> 00:44:22.400
I really do love Australia.

1195
00:44:22.740 --> 00:44:24.960
Sydney is quite fantastic as a city.

1196
00:44:25.440 --> 00:44:26.840
It's really just beautiful.

1197
00:44:26.840 --> 00:44:28.340
And it's just sort of got my heart.

1198
00:44:28.460 --> 00:44:32.500
Bondi Beach has got my heart, which is extraordinary for someone who is pale and ginger.

1199
00:44:32.500 --> 00:44:40.340
I would never go swimming, you know, before nine o'clock at night or, you know, after five o'clock in the morning.

1200
00:44:40.880 --> 00:44:42.440
Great times to avoid sharks.

1201
00:44:43.900 --> 00:44:45.060
Feeding time for the sharks.

1202
00:44:45.180 --> 00:44:45.300
Feeding time.

1203
00:44:45.560 --> 00:44:46.000
Feeding time.

1204
00:44:46.280 --> 00:44:49.660
Bondi Beach is my friend's absolute favourite place on the planet.

1205
00:44:49.780 --> 00:44:53.360
It's really genuinely got my heart in a way that I never thought it did.

1206
00:44:53.360 --> 00:45:01.860
And, you know, I've been to some really fantastic places, but for properly what has your heart, it's Bondi.

1207
00:45:02.340 --> 00:45:05.580
Did you go there on holiday or work or how did you find it?

1208
00:45:05.720 --> 00:45:11.120
No, I've been there for work a couple of times because what I didn't realise, I wish someone had told me,

1209
00:45:11.160 --> 00:45:16.140
I wish someone had told me years and years ago that I was pretty well known in Australia and New Zealand.

1210
00:45:16.140 --> 00:45:22.500
I had genuinely no idea and I went over and toured one of my shows, my comedy shows, and it was like being a rock star.

1211
00:45:22.680 --> 00:45:27.220
I was playing stadiums and I was just like, why didn't anyone tell me?

1212
00:45:27.560 --> 00:45:30.420
Because I genuinely would have moved to Australia years and years ago.

1213
00:45:31.160 --> 00:45:35.240
So I've been out there a few times and then I've just done a show out in Australia called Queen of Oz.

1214
00:45:35.420 --> 00:45:38.840
So we went and we lived about six, seven months.

1215
00:45:38.840 --> 00:45:46.580
And so it was just, yeah, it'd never been a place where I was thinking, well, because it's so far, you know, it's such an obvious thing to say, but it's a schlep.

1216
00:45:47.280 --> 00:45:50.000
But then when I got there, I just couldn't believe how much I loved it.

1217
00:45:50.300 --> 00:45:55.520
In fact, sometimes me and my husband go, because he's from LA and I'm from London, I mean, it's hardly really meeting in the middle.

1218
00:45:55.720 --> 00:45:57.960
But, you know, I've worked out meeting in the middle.

1219
00:45:58.100 --> 00:45:59.620
I'm saying it's somewhere like Boston.

1220
00:46:00.420 --> 00:46:04.700
But we go, well, maybe just, you know, because LA is his, London is mine.

1221
00:46:05.240 --> 00:46:06.860
Let's have Australia for ourselves.

1222
00:46:07.040 --> 00:46:08.620
You know, let's let Sydney be ours.

1223
00:46:08.980 --> 00:46:10.620
Oh, that's so romantic.

1224
00:46:11.020 --> 00:46:11.720
It's very romantic.

1225
00:46:12.040 --> 00:46:13.120
It'll never happen, but it's nice.

1226
00:46:14.580 --> 00:46:15.180
All right.

1227
00:46:15.360 --> 00:46:15.840
Let's see.

1228
00:46:16.020 --> 00:46:16.640
Next question.

1229
00:46:17.220 --> 00:46:19.000
What do you like to do on the weekends?

1230
00:46:19.500 --> 00:46:24.420
I think mainly in my life, I'm defined more by what I don't do and what I don't like by what I do.

1231
00:46:24.520 --> 00:46:26.920
If you ask me what I like, I'd go, I'd struggle.

1232
00:46:27.080 --> 00:46:29.480
But if you ask me what I don't like, we'd be here all day.

1233
00:46:29.640 --> 00:46:31.720
So I can tell you what I don't do at the weekend.

1234
00:46:31.940 --> 00:46:32.900
Yeah, I love it.

1235
00:46:33.860 --> 00:46:34.220
Cook.

1236
00:46:34.700 --> 00:46:36.820
I don't like to cook at all.

1237
00:46:36.940 --> 00:46:37.580
It's not just the weekends.

1238
00:46:38.840 --> 00:46:40.980
Which baffles me why I've just been offered a cooking show.

1239
00:46:42.500 --> 00:46:45.660
I think someone heard me on the radio talking about how much I hate to cook.

1240
00:46:45.720 --> 00:46:47.560
And they went, we should actually put this on TV.

1241
00:46:47.780 --> 00:46:51.820
And it's like, I'm not sure you quite understood my feelings about not liking to cook.

1242
00:46:51.820 --> 00:46:53.360
I would watch you hate cooking.

1243
00:46:53.600 --> 00:46:55.300
Oh, it's not even hating.

1244
00:46:55.480 --> 00:46:59.060
It's proper, like, it's like a primal, it gives me rage.

1245
00:47:00.640 --> 00:47:02.720
Proper, like, rage, this idea.

1246
00:47:02.940 --> 00:47:05.020
And it's what I find doubly awful.

1247
00:47:05.140 --> 00:47:08.960
It's like with a family and children, you're expected to do it three times a day.

1248
00:47:09.100 --> 00:47:09.400
Uh-huh.

1249
00:47:09.400 --> 00:47:11.300
And I find that astonishing.

1250
00:47:12.020 --> 00:47:16.020
And that's why I'm a huge advocate for breakfast cereals three times a day.

1251
00:47:16.140 --> 00:47:17.120
I mean, because that's what I would eat.

1252
00:47:17.200 --> 00:47:18.400
I'm not, I digress.

1253
00:47:18.760 --> 00:47:19.080
Okay.

1254
00:47:19.280 --> 00:47:20.420
I'm not cooking at the weekend.

1255
00:47:20.560 --> 00:47:20.840
You're not cooking.

1256
00:47:20.840 --> 00:47:22.460
I'm not cooking any day, to be honeSt.

1257
00:47:22.580 --> 00:47:23.300
Mama don't cook.

1258
00:47:23.580 --> 00:47:25.680
It's literally, I've got a T-shirt going, Mama don't cook.

1259
00:47:25.820 --> 00:47:27.120
So don't come up with me that I'm hungry.

1260
00:47:27.780 --> 00:47:31.460
If you want pure rage, ask me for a snack.

1261
00:47:31.920 --> 00:47:32.200
Right.

1262
00:47:32.780 --> 00:47:34.380
Oh, it infuriates me.

1263
00:47:34.440 --> 00:47:35.440
It really does.

1264
00:47:35.520 --> 00:47:41.520
And in a strange way, because I didn't think I was so un-maternal that I just didn't have

1265
00:47:41.520 --> 00:47:43.880
the instinct to give people nourishment.

1266
00:47:44.240 --> 00:47:45.360
But I clearly do.

1267
00:47:45.620 --> 00:47:46.380
Yeah, no, awful.

1268
00:47:46.580 --> 00:47:47.820
God, I can't, I hate cooking.

1269
00:47:48.360 --> 00:47:49.700
I don't want to exercise.

1270
00:47:52.160 --> 00:47:56.600
You know, I don't want to, I don't mind ambling about, but I, yeah, I don't want to do that.

1271
00:47:56.840 --> 00:47:57.760
I don't want to socialize.

1272
00:47:59.780 --> 00:48:03.500
So don't ask me to your barbecue and expect me to throw something on it.

1273
00:48:03.540 --> 00:48:04.260
That's not happening.

1274
00:48:04.560 --> 00:48:07.720
I just like, think I'm actually, I'm quite a natural hermit.

1275
00:48:08.460 --> 00:48:10.460
I'm a natural loner.

1276
00:48:10.560 --> 00:48:12.040
I'm definitely not a pack animal.

1277
00:48:12.620 --> 00:48:13.800
I'm a loner.

1278
00:48:13.980 --> 00:48:14.920
I'm a lone wolf.

1279
00:48:17.120 --> 00:48:24.000
And my weekends are, if I had my own way, I would sit in front of Netflix or the TV.

1280
00:48:24.340 --> 00:48:26.420
I'm sure other subscription services are available.

1281
00:48:27.140 --> 00:48:29.120
And eat stuff that I don't have to cook.

1282
00:48:30.040 --> 00:48:31.060
That sounds lovely.

1283
00:48:31.360 --> 00:48:31.940
That sounds like a great weekend.

1284
00:48:32.820 --> 00:48:33.000
Yeah.

1285
00:48:33.660 --> 00:48:35.060
And read astrology things.

1286
00:48:35.200 --> 00:48:36.260
Read astrology blogs.

1287
00:48:36.440 --> 00:48:37.220
Because I love an astrology.

1288
00:48:37.400 --> 00:48:37.900
Yeah, I love that.

1289
00:48:38.080 --> 00:48:39.020
What is your sign?

1290
00:48:39.540 --> 00:48:39.900
Sagittarius.

1291
00:48:40.180 --> 00:48:40.940
Okay, I'm Pisces.

1292
00:48:41.240 --> 00:48:41.900
Oh, you are?

1293
00:48:42.000 --> 00:48:42.640
I'm a Cancer.

1294
00:48:42.960 --> 00:48:43.300
You are.

1295
